# Area: tab (new area dir; app/ precedent — P-TAB-001's slice files live under
#       chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/ but are tracked separately from P-APP-001's
#       app/ patches; area-deviation recorded here per patches/README conventions).
# Rationale: First seam of the browser-less tab model. Content consults
#   ChromeContentBrowserClient::GetWebContentsViewDelegate synchronously inside
#   WebContents::Create (content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc:4537)
#   and at four later call sites (:3476/:3629/:3662/:3775), so the embedded-mode
#   decision must be ambient — post-Create tagging is too late (P-TAB-001-SLICES
#   §3). Adds rearc::IsEngineEmbeddedMode() plus ReArcWebContentsViewDelegate
#   (additive, under chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/) and the ~5-line upstream
#   branch in chrome_content_browser_client.cc.
# Gate: Branch taken only when rearc::IsEngineEmbeddedMode() is true, i.e. a
#   ReArc lifecycle host is installed (P-APP-001 app/002). Standalone Chromium
#   takes the stock path bit-identically.
# Deviation from plan (recorded in P-TAB-001-SLICES.md drift log): the slice
#   plan sketched an explicit std::atomic<bool> + SetEngineEmbeddedMode() set
#   from rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm. That file is created by patch app/002 and
#   frozen by the series-mechanics invariant (later patches never modify
#   earlier patches' files), so no legal setter site exists. The predicate is
#   derived instead: GetEngineLifecycleHost() != nullptr — identical
#   semantics, same source of truth as every P-APP-001 gate.
# Hunk placement (series mechanics): the upstream-file hunks sit in
#   chrome_content_browser_client.cc (untouched by any other patch) and in
#   chrome/browser/BUILD.gn between "icon_loader_mac.mm" and
#   "memory_details_mac.cc" — NOT at the alphabetical position after
